1
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:52,900
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,350 --> 00:00:55,990
[Episode 21]

3
00:01:02,390 --> 00:01:04,620
Wait. Why'd you flip my car over?

4
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:06,500
You little punk.

5
00:01:07,140 --> 00:01:08,480
You sold me counterfeit cigarettes,

6
00:01:08,480 --> 00:01:09,350
didn't you?

7
00:01:09,350 --> 00:01:10,180
Boss. Boss. Boss.

8
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:10,930
Boss, I'm sorry.

9
00:01:10,930 --> 00:01:12,260
You thought I'd never had real Zhonghua,
so you could rip me off?

10
00:01:12,260 --> 00:01:13,560
I've never smoked real ones either, Boss.

11
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:14,870
I was just trying to scrape together
some dowry for my sister.

12
00:01:14,870 --> 00:01:15,789
Please, Boss, let me off this once.

13
00:01:15,789 --> 00:01:16,420
I'm sorry, Boss.

14
00:01:16,420 --> 00:01:17,870
Do you have any idea

15
00:01:17,870 --> 00:01:18,789
how much I had to pay out last week?

16
00:01:18,789 --> 00:01:19,210
-Boss!
-Don't move!

17
00:01:19,210 --> 00:01:20,460
Please, Boss. You can't touch that money.

18
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:20,950
Boss.

19
00:01:20,950 --> 00:01:22,060
Don't struggle.
You'll only make it worse. Don't move.

20
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:22,950
Boss, Boss,

21
00:01:22,970 --> 00:01:25,360
I'm sorry. Please let me off, Boss.

22
00:01:25,710 --> 00:01:26,980
Please. You can't take that money, Boss.

23
00:01:28,039 --> 00:01:29,730
I've already called the cops.

24
00:01:29,930 --> 00:01:30,930
Figure it out yourself.

25
00:01:30,930 --> 00:01:31,710
Boss.

26
00:01:31,730 --> 00:01:32,289
Wait.

27
00:01:36,789 --> 00:01:37,670
Boss,

28
00:01:37,830 --> 00:01:39,140
please let me off this once.

29
00:01:39,940 --> 00:01:41,259
I'm begging you.

30
00:01:41,650 --> 00:01:42,530
Boss.

31
00:01:43,090 --> 00:01:44,009
Boss.

32
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:51,740
These auto repair guys
are pretty ruthless.

33
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:06,790
Hey, what's up?

34
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:08,080
Yang,

35
00:02:08,620 --> 00:02:10,150
I'm screwed.

36
00:02:10,639 --> 00:02:12,030
Good thing I had you, Yang.

37
00:02:13,250 --> 00:02:14,240
When the cops come,

38
00:02:14,490 --> 00:02:16,120
if they ask you anything,
just say you don't know.

39
00:02:18,640 --> 00:02:19,990
Without the cigarettes,
they can't charge you.

40
00:02:24,130 --> 00:02:25,550
Without the cigarettes,
they can't charge me.

41
00:02:27,130 --> 00:02:27,710
Here.

42
00:02:28,090 --> 00:02:29,050
Take this and report back to Dong.

43
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:34,300
Thanks.

44
00:02:40,510 --> 00:02:42,460
You're a real brother-in-law.

45
00:02:45,840 --> 00:02:47,460
Hold it properly.

46
00:02:47,690 --> 00:02:49,340
If you drop it,
I'll break your hand.

47
00:02:50,250 --> 00:02:51,770
San Yan'er,

48
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:53,680
have you gotten too big
for your britches?

49
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:55,160
How dare you sell counterfeit cigarettes?

50
00:02:53,790 --> 00:03:00,420
[Fortune-Bringing Arowana]

51
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:56,250
Dong,

52
00:02:56,870 --> 00:02:58,060
the money's back.

53
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:00,510
So I guess that makes us even, right?

54
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:01,560
What do you mean, "we're even"?

55
00:03:01,010 --> 00:03:04,690
[Fortune-Bringing Arowana]

56
00:03:02,180 --> 00:03:03,070
What do you mean by that?

57
00:03:03,180 --> 00:03:04,500
Tell me. Where are my real cigarettes?

58
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:07,620
Well,

59
00:03:09,860 --> 00:03:12,430
the real ones were mixed in
with the counterfeit ones.

60
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:15,280
So Liu Yang had them taken away
and burned.

61
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:16,300
Who?

62
00:03:16,470 --> 00:03:17,240
Liu Yang?

63
00:03:17,870 --> 00:03:18,840
Your buddy?

64
00:03:19,430 --> 00:03:21,370
I've never liked that guy, you know?

65
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:23,400
He's way too blunt.

66
00:03:23,430 --> 00:03:25,280
Is there something wrong
with his head or what?

67
00:03:25,280 --> 00:03:26,620
He once got caught in a wildfire.

68
00:03:26,620 --> 00:03:27,800
What the hell's that got to do with me?

69
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:29,000
Stay away from him,

70
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:29,840
got it?

71
00:03:30,650 --> 00:03:31,560
No, Dong.

72
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:33,020
He was just trying to help.

73
00:03:34,079 --> 00:03:35,640
His sister's a cop,

74
00:03:35,780 --> 00:03:36,530
so he knows the law.

75
00:03:37,060 --> 00:03:39,500
He said they can't convict me
unless they catch me with the evidence,

76
00:03:39,500 --> 00:03:40,990
so he had them burned.

77
00:03:42,010 --> 00:03:43,360
His sister's a cop?

78
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,170
So what,

79
00:03:47,780 --> 00:03:49,140
you've got yourself a new backer now?

80
00:03:49,210 --> 00:03:49,780
No!

81
00:03:49,780 --> 00:03:50,410
No, no, no.

82
00:03:50,410 --> 00:03:51,360
That's not it, Dong.

83
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:53,120
I keep you fed, I keep you supplied,

84
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:55,079
and you rat me out to the cops?

85
00:03:55,079 --> 00:03:57,410
Fine, then. Go work with the cops.

86
00:03:57,410 --> 00:03:58,960
Go run with Liu Yang.

87
00:03:58,960 --> 00:03:59,690
No, Dong.

88
00:03:59,690 --> 00:04:00,520
It's not like that.

89
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:01,190
No, no, no.

90
00:04:01,190 --> 00:04:02,000
Never.

91
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:02,950
All right.

92
00:04:03,150 --> 00:04:05,030
Leave the car and the keys with me

93
00:04:05,030 --> 00:04:06,080
when you go.

94
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:07,280
And don't sell cigarettes anymore.

95
00:04:07,810 --> 00:04:09,410
I don't trust you.

96
00:04:09,530 --> 00:04:10,500
Don't, Dong.

97
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:11,280
Please.

98
00:04:11,280 --> 00:04:12,470
J-Just give me one more chance, will you?

99
00:04:12,470 --> 00:04:13,370
Just one last chance.

100
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:14,240
Please, Dong.

101
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:15,400
Cut me some slack.

102
00:04:16,190 --> 00:04:16,920
Dong, please, please.

103
00:04:20,630 --> 00:04:21,480
San Yan'er,

104
00:04:22,660 --> 00:04:25,420
why can't you do anything right?

105
00:04:28,220 --> 00:04:29,370
You still wanna run with me?

106
00:04:31,310 --> 00:04:32,420
I've got a buddy

107
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,130
who runs a nightclub in Guangzhou.

108
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:35,500
Go stay there for a couple of days.

109
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:37,060
Don't come back for a while.

110
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:38,240
Got it, Dong.

111
00:04:38,690 --> 00:04:39,890
Go ahead, laugh.

112
00:04:39,890 --> 00:04:40,690
No, no, I won't.

113
00:04:41,070 --> 00:04:42,430
Did I tell you to put it down?

114
00:04:42,830 --> 00:04:43,659
Keep holding it.

115
00:04:43,659 --> 00:04:44,580
Okay, I won't smile.

116
00:04:44,830 --> 00:04:45,880
Okay. I'm not smiling. I'm not.

117
00:04:48,250 --> 00:04:49,240
Guangzhou.

118
00:04:53,690 --> 00:04:54,890
Can I put it down now, Dong?

119
00:04:55,890 --> 00:04:57,070
Hold it until the girls come in
for their shift.

120
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:04,930
Just for one day.

121
00:05:05,270 --> 00:05:05,930
How much is it?

122
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:08,810
Mercedes.

123
00:05:16,390 --> 00:05:16,980
Okay.

124
00:05:17,630 --> 00:05:18,300
Let me think about it.

125
00:05:18,300 --> 00:05:20,070
I'll call you back.

126
00:05:20,750 --> 00:05:21,270
Alright.

127
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:22,420
Okay, okay.

128
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:26,950
[General Manager]

129
00:05:23,270 --> 00:05:24,390
You need a car,

130
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:26,370
and it has to be a Mercedes?

131
00:05:28,810 --> 00:05:30,160
Doesn't the company have cars?

132
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:36,000
It's a family matter. I don't want
to use a car from the company.

133
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,300
What family matter?

134
00:05:39,810 --> 00:05:41,210
Just take it.

135
00:05:41,420 --> 00:05:43,190
You've been driving it
to see your girlfriend every day,

136
00:05:43,190 --> 00:05:44,180
and I never said a word.

137
00:05:52,430 --> 00:05:53,480
Your zipper's down.

138
00:06:00,620 --> 00:06:01,660
What family matter could there be

139
00:06:01,660 --> 00:06:02,740
that you need a Mercedes for?

140
00:06:06,630 --> 00:06:07,370
A wedding.

141
00:06:10,510 --> 00:06:11,330
Whose wedding is it?

142
00:06:21,750 --> 00:06:22,430
Mine.

143
00:06:32,860 --> 00:06:34,680
So if I don't ask,
you weren't planning on telling me?

144
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:44,190
You're always walking around
with my hair on your clothes.

145
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:47,900
I'm guessing she figured out
our relationship a long time ago.

146
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:51,770
To put up with you

147
00:06:51,770 --> 00:06:53,390
and even marry you just to get a kidney...

148
00:06:55,130 --> 00:06:56,570
She's quite something.

149
00:07:03,970 --> 00:07:05,490
She's different from us.

150
00:07:10,810 --> 00:07:13,770
Taking on a burden like this so young—

151
00:07:14,310 --> 00:07:15,430
what for?

152
00:07:37,250 --> 00:07:38,070
True love.

153
00:07:38,070 --> 00:07:39,159
True love my ass.

154
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:52,570
Then congratulations
on finding true love.

155
00:07:54,840 --> 00:07:56,810
I'll give you a big red envelope
at your wedding.

156
00:08:13,930 --> 00:08:14,860
How much is this car?

157
00:08:15,570 --> 00:08:17,120
-For rent, I mean.
-It's 2,000 yuan to rent it out.

158
00:08:17,630 --> 00:08:18,420
What do you need it for?

159
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:20,070
A wedding.

160
00:08:20,070 --> 00:08:20,800
Sure.

161
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:27,750
Can I take a look inside?

162
00:08:35,740 --> 00:08:37,169
How much is the one in the middle?

163
00:08:37,409 --> 00:08:39,169
That one in the middle is 2,800 yuan.

164
00:08:52,290 --> 00:08:53,290
If I rent it,

165
00:08:53,320 --> 00:08:55,480
does that include all the decorations?

166
00:08:55,480 --> 00:08:56,440
Those are charged separately.

167
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:03,170
What about a driver?

168
00:09:03,170 --> 00:09:04,390
A driver isn't included.
That's charged separately.

169
00:09:05,850 --> 00:09:06,720
Just a moment.

170
00:09:07,290 --> 00:09:07,960
Ma'am.

171
00:09:08,910 --> 00:09:09,900
Ma'am, ma'am.

172
00:09:10,360 --> 00:09:11,840
Ma'am, please don't do that.

173
00:09:11,840 --> 00:09:13,470
This is a brand-new car.

174
00:09:13,700 --> 00:09:15,010
So what if it's new?

175
00:09:15,150 --> 00:09:16,360
It's expensive.

176
00:09:19,130 --> 00:09:19,740
What,

177
00:09:20,050 --> 00:09:21,130
are you buying it?

178
00:09:22,670 --> 00:09:24,240
Driving a convertible
around Northeast China?

179
00:09:25,290 --> 00:09:26,900
The wind'll blow your face sideways.

180
00:09:30,170 --> 00:09:31,140
I like it.

181
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:43,620
Where are you going?
I'll give you a ride.

182
00:09:43,620 --> 00:09:45,590
Yuhong Square.

183
00:09:47,030 --> 00:09:48,290
What are you going there for?

184
00:09:48,290 --> 00:09:49,220
None of your business.

185
00:09:49,840 --> 00:09:51,340
Just drop me off and go.

186
00:09:51,340 --> 00:09:53,230
You can keep the car for a couple of days.

187
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:22,120
Welcome.

188
00:10:22,720 --> 00:10:24,130
Come on in. Have a seat inside.

189
00:10:28,510 --> 00:10:29,390
Hello, ma'am.

190
00:10:30,450 --> 00:10:31,270
Would you like

191
00:10:31,790 --> 00:10:33,320
a shampoo or a haircut?

192
00:10:49,460 --> 00:10:50,290
I'd like a hair treatment.

193
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:51,500
Sure.

194
00:10:54,410 --> 00:10:55,510
Is the water temperature okay?

195
00:10:59,770 --> 00:11:01,150
How's the pressure?

196
00:11:02,890 --> 00:11:03,860
It's perfect.

197
00:11:05,740 --> 00:11:06,940
If I were a man,

198
00:11:06,940 --> 00:11:08,510
I'd come here every day
to get my hair washed.

199
00:11:12,030 --> 00:11:13,740
Ma'am, you're teasing me.

200
00:11:15,150 --> 00:11:16,700
Ma'am, what kind of treatment

201
00:11:16,700 --> 00:11:17,840
do you want today?

202
00:11:18,030 --> 00:11:24,150
[Bangs Trim: 2 yuan] [Haircut: 3 yuan]
[Wash & Blow-Dry: 3 yuan]

203
00:11:18,820 --> 00:11:20,290
We've got different options
at different prices.

204
00:11:21,220 --> 00:11:22,580
You decide.

205
00:11:22,790 --> 00:11:24,000
I'm going to a wedding.

206
00:11:24,290 --> 00:11:25,410
Whose wedding is it?

207
00:11:26,030 --> 00:11:27,030
It's such a small place around here.

208
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:28,890
Maybe I even know them.

209
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,480
Ma'am, your skin is so nice.

210
00:11:45,580 --> 00:11:46,900
But what's that scar

211
00:11:47,460 --> 00:11:48,860
on your forehead?

212
00:11:49,530 --> 00:11:50,650
How'd you get it?

213
00:12:00,250 --> 00:12:01,320
Ma'am, are you married?

214
00:12:02,700 --> 00:12:04,010
My husband just died.

215
00:12:30,510 --> 00:12:31,480
I'm doing legit business here.

216
00:12:32,710 --> 00:12:34,020
Come back later.

217
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:36,130
What, you're doing legit work now?

218
00:12:55,900 --> 00:12:57,410
Do you live nearby, ma'am?

219
00:13:02,300 --> 00:13:03,810
I don't mean anything by it.

220
00:13:03,910 --> 00:13:05,100
I just noticed

221
00:13:05,840 --> 00:13:06,650
you seem to like

222
00:13:06,650 --> 00:13:08,620
getting your hair permed and dyed.

223
00:13:08,770 --> 00:13:10,410
Why not come get your hair treatments here
more often?

224
00:13:11,490 --> 00:13:12,850
You could get a membership card.

225
00:13:13,270 --> 00:13:14,410
I'll give you a discount.

226
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:16,270
It's a good deal.

227
00:13:24,860 --> 00:13:25,650
Sure.

228
00:13:43,700 --> 00:13:44,650
Come to think of it,

229
00:13:44,650 --> 00:13:46,890
my husband probably
had a membership card here.

230
00:13:46,910 --> 00:13:48,190
His name was Li Dewu.

231
00:13:48,720 --> 00:13:50,440
Could you check the balance on his card

232
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:52,090
if there's enough for today's treatment?

233
00:14:17,990 --> 00:14:19,360
What are you doing here?

234
00:14:19,460 --> 00:14:21,250
I brought you something to eat.

235
00:14:21,250 --> 00:14:22,440
I... I'm not hungry.

236
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:23,840
See? I've still got a customer.

237
00:14:23,840 --> 00:14:24,360
You should head home.

238
00:14:24,360 --> 00:14:25,790
Pork belly braised with green beans.
It's delicious.

239
00:14:25,790 --> 00:14:26,460
I've brought you some.

240
00:14:26,460 --> 00:14:27,270
Have a bite. Here,

241
00:14:27,300 --> 00:14:28,160
try some.

242
00:14:30,050 --> 00:14:30,580
Okay.

243
00:14:32,340 --> 00:14:32,870
Good, huh?

244
00:14:32,870 --> 00:14:33,320
Yeah, it's good.

245
00:14:33,820 --> 00:14:34,550
You should go.

246
00:14:34,550 --> 00:14:35,600
I... I'm not hungry.

247
00:14:36,130 --> 00:14:37,040
Just leave it here.

248
00:14:37,150 --> 00:14:38,340
Make sure you eat it later.

249
00:14:38,340 --> 00:14:38,840
I will.

250
00:14:39,790 --> 00:14:40,460
Money.

251
00:14:41,960 --> 00:14:43,000
Here's what I made driving this week.

252
00:14:43,340 --> 00:14:44,890
It's 20 yuan less than last week—

253
00:14:44,890 --> 00:14:45,870
I bought them drinks.

254
00:14:45,870 --> 00:14:46,770
All right, I got it.

255
00:14:46,770 --> 00:14:48,040
-I'm heading out, honey.
-You go ahead.

256
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:21,340
Please set up
a new membership card for me.

257
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:25,600
[Happiness]

258
00:15:23,870 --> 00:15:24,960
Let's welcome the newlyweds

259
00:15:24,960 --> 00:15:28,840
to pour champagne into the champagne tower
and toast to their love.

260
00:15:28,870 --> 00:15:29,290
Friends,

261
00:15:29,290 --> 00:15:30,530
let's wish them

262
00:15:30,530 --> 00:15:32,100
a happy marriage

263
00:15:32,100 --> 00:15:33,570
and a lifetime of happiness together.

264
00:15:34,010 --> 00:15:35,170
Now, let's have the newlyweds

265
00:15:35,170 --> 00:15:37,000
share a traditional cross-cup toast.

266
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,330
-A big cross-cup toast!
-A big cross-cup toast!

267
00:15:38,460 --> 00:15:39,720
-A big cross-cup toast!
-A big cross-cup toast!

268
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:43,850
-A big cross-cup toast!
-A big cross-cup toast!

269
00:15:45,700 --> 00:15:48,100
Let's wish the newlyweds

270
00:15:48,170 --> 00:15:49,720
everlasting love

271
00:15:49,720 --> 00:15:52,130
and happiness.

272
00:15:52,870 --> 00:15:54,290
-Kiss!
-Kiss!

273
00:15:54,290 --> 00:15:57,100
-Kiss!
-Kiss!

274
00:15:57,100 --> 00:15:59,960
-Kiss!
-Kiss!

275
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:02,840
-Kiss!
-Kiss!

276
00:16:02,840 --> 00:16:06,370
-Kiss!
-Kiss!

277
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:11,170
-Kiss!
-Kiss!

278
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:14,770
Nice!

279
00:16:14,870 --> 00:16:15,600
Nice!

